      "Mark-Sweep-Compact: Standard in Old Generation to prevent fragmentation and allow simple bump-the-pointer allocations.",
      "Two-Finger vs Lisp2 Compaction: Lisp2 sliding compaction preserves object allocation order in memory.",
      "Generational Alignment: 98% of objects die young, making Mark-Copy ideal for Young Gen; surviving objects live long, making Compact ideal for Old Gen."
