    "visualDiagram": "\n          <div class=\"visual-diagram-box\">\n            <div class=\"diagram-header-label\">\ud83e\udde0 Visual Mental Model: Object Lifecycle Across Generational Boundaries</div>\n            <div class=\"flow-chain\">\n              <div class=\"flow-step-node node-blue\" style=\"min-width: 140px;\">\n                <span class=\"node-label\">Eden Space</span>\n                <span class=\"node-desc\">New Allocations</span>\n              </div>\n              <span class=\"flow-arrow-separator\">\u2500\u2500Minor GC\u2500\u2500\u25ba</span>\n              <div class=\"flow-step-node node-orange\" style=\"min-width: 150px;\">\n                <span class=\"node-label\">Survivor S0 \u25c4\u25ba S1</span>\n                <span class=\"node-desc\">Age Stamped in MarkWord</span>\n              </div>\n              <span class=\"flow-arrow-separator\">\u2500\u2500Age &gt;= 15\u2500\u2500\u25ba</span>\n              <div class=\"flow-step-node node-green\" style=\"min-width: 150px;\">\n                <span class=\"node-label\">Tenured (Old Gen)</span>\n                <span class=\"node-desc\">Long-lived Singletons</span>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.78rem; color: #a855f7; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;\">\n              <span>\u26a1</span> <strong>Card Table & Remembered Sets:</strong> Old-to-Young references tracked via Card Table dirty bits to avoid full Old Gen scans during Minor GC!\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        ",
    "internalWorking": "Young Generation consists of Eden and two Survivor spaces (S0 From, S1 To), typically with an 8:1:1 ratio (-XX:SurvivorRatio=8). (1) Minor GC: When Eden fills, a Minor GC triggers. Live objects in Eden and active Survivor (S0) are copied to the empty Survivor (S1). Their object header age bit increments by 1. The roles of S0 and S1 swap. (2) Tenuring Threshold: When an object's age reaches -XX:MaxTenuringThreshold (default 15, because age field in 64-bit Mark Word is 4 bits: max 1111 = 15), it is promoted to Old Generation. (3) Dynamic Age Calculation: If the cumulative size of surviving objects in a Survivor space exceeds 50% (-XX:TargetSurvivorRatio), all objects with age >= that cohort are promoted early.",
    "complexPart": "The Card Table and Post-Write Barrier: During Minor GC, scanning the entire multi-gigabyte Old Gen to find references into Eden would destroy pause time guarantees. The JVM solves this using a Card Table (byte array where 1 byte represents a 512-byte card of Old Gen). Whenever an Old Gen reference is updated ('oldObj.field = youngObj'), the JIT emits a post-write barrier that marks that card as DIRTY (0x01). Minor GC only scans the dirty cards in the Card Table, keeping pauses minimal.",
